From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roja Eswaran <roja@zededa.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:09:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/9pfs: allow opening special files

EVE gives each container app its root filesystem over 9p (fsdriver local,
security_model=none). Since the fix for CVE-2023-2861, openat_file()
refuses to open anything that is neither a regular file nor a directory.
EVE has run without that check since container apps broke on 9p with it
(lf-edge/eve#4186).

This reopens CVE-2023-2861: a guest that can create or reach a device node
in the exported tree can open the host device behind it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [reverts a CVE fix]
Signed-off-by: Roja Eswaran <roja@zededa.com>
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 hw/9pfs/9p-util.h | 41 -----------------------------------------
 1 file changed, 41 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/9pfs/9p-util.h b/hw/9pfs/9p-util.h
index 8dfa803..a00b552 100644
--- a/hw/9pfs/9p-util.h
+++ b/hw/9pfs/9p-util.h
@@ -121,38 +121,6 @@ static inline void close_preserve_errno(int fd)
     errno = serrno;
 }
 
-/**
- * close_if_special_file() - Close @fd if neither regular file nor directory.
- *
- * @fd: file descriptor of open file
- * Return: 0 on regular file or directory, -1 otherwise
- *
- * CVE-2023-2861: Prohibit opening any special file directly on host
- * (especially device files), as a compromised client could potentially gain
- * access outside exported tree under certain, unsafe setups. We expect
- * client to handle I/O on special files exclusively on guest side.
- */
-static inline int close_if_special_file(int fd)
-{
-    struct stat stbuf;
-
-    if (qemu_fstat(fd, &stbuf) < 0) {
-        close_preserve_errno(fd);
-        return -1;
-    }
-    if (!S_ISREG(stbuf.st_mode) && !S_ISDIR(stbuf.st_mode)) {
-        error_report_once(
-            "9p: broken or compromised client detected; attempt to open "
-            "special file (i.e. neither regular file, nor directory)"
-        );
-        close(fd);
-        errno = ENXIO;
-        return -1;
-    }
-
-    return 0;
-}
-
 static inline int openat_dir(int dirfd, const char *name)
 {
     return qemu_openat(dirfd, name,
@@ -189,15 +157,6 @@ again:
 
     /* Only if O_PATH is not set ... */
     if (!(flags & O_PATH_9P_UTIL)) {
-        /*
-         * Prevent I/O on special files (device files, etc.) on host side,
-         * however it is safe and required to allow opening them with O_PATH,
-         * as this is limited to (required) path based operations only.
-         */
-        if (close_if_special_file(fd) < 0) {
-            return -1;
-        }
-
         serrno = errno;
         /*
          * O_NONBLOCK was only needed to open the file. Let's drop it. We don't
